@startuml
title Proof of Collaboration (PoCol) Reward Distribution and Verification in Round r
skinparam dpi 180
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
participant "Miner A (registered miner)" as A
participant "Miner B (winner miner)" as B
participant "Miner C (registered miner)" as C
participant "Blockchain ledger" as L

B -> B: Detect nonce value for which the cryptographic hash\nof the candidate block header combined with this nonce value\nis below the difficulty target in round r
B -> B: Construct a provisional block for round r\ncontaining the candidate block header, the winning nonce value,\nand the list of selected transactions\n(excluding the reward distribution transaction for now)
B -> B: Read the registered miner set for round r\nfrom the local view of the blockchain ledger\n(for example: Miner A, Miner B, Miner C, and possibly others)
B -> B: Apply the Proof of Collaboration reward distribution function\nusing as input:\n- the registered miner set for round r,\n- the expected block reward for round r,\n- the total transaction fees included in the provisional block,\n- and any additional collaboration metrics defined by the protocol\nOutput:\n- a reward share for each registered miner in the current round
B -> B: Verify locally that the sum of all computed reward shares\nis equal to the expected block reward for round r\nplus the total transaction fees collected in the provisional block
B -> B: Create a reward distribution transaction for round r\ncontaining multiple outputs, one for each registered miner,\nwhere each output pays the corresponding reward share\nto the payment address of that miner\n(for example, outputs for Miner A, Miner B, Miner C, and all others\nin the registered miner set)
B -> B: Insert the reward distribution transaction\ninto the list of transactions of the provisional block\nso that the block now consists of:\n- the candidate block header,\n- the winning nonce value,\n- the reward distribution transaction,\n- and all other included transactions
B -> A: Broadcast the new block for round r\nwith the winning nonce value and the reward distribution transaction\nto Miner A
B -> C: Broadcast the new block for round r\nwith the winning nonce value and the reward distribution transaction\nto Miner C
A -> A: Verify the received block for round r by checking:\n- the validity of the block header and the winning nonce value\n  (Proof of Work below the difficulty target),\n- the validity of all ordinary transactions in the block,\n- the correctness of the reward distribution transaction, including:\n  (1) all beneficiaries correspond exactly to miners in the\n      registered miner set for round r,\n  (2) each registered miner receives exactly the share\n      prescribed by the Proof of Collaboration reward distribution function,\n  (3) the sum of all reward outputs equals the expected block reward\n      plus the total collected transaction fees,\n  (4) no extra value is created or destroyed
C -> C: Perform the same verification procedure for the received block\nfor round r, including full verification of the reward distribution transaction
B -> B: Re-verify locally that the block, including the reward distribution,\nremains consistent before committing it to the local blockchain ledger
A -> L: Append the new valid block for round r\nwith the reward distribution transaction\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner A
B -> L: Append the new valid block for round r\nwith the reward distribution transaction\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner B
C -> L: Append the new valid block for round r\nwith the reward distribution transaction\nto the local view of the blockchain ledger of Miner C
A -> A: Update the local balances of all miners\naccording to the reward outputs recorded in the new block\n(for example, increase the balance of Miner A by its reward share\nand update the balances of Miner B, Miner C, and all other miners)
B -> B: Update the local balances of all miners\naccording to the same reward outputs in the new block
C -> C: Update the local balances of all miners\naccording to the same reward outputs in the new block
A -> A: Use the updated blockchain state, including\nnew balances and any changes to the registered miner set,\nas input for the next Proof of Collaboration consensus round
B -> B: Use the updated blockchain state as input\nfor the next Proof of Collaboration consensus round
C -> C: Use the updated blockchain state as input\nfor the next Proof of Collaboration consensus round\n(if Miner C remains a registered miner and continues to participate)
@enduml
